Group calls, ours (not whatsapp-light's); applied by scripts/hypermeow-work.sh after meowcaller.patch.
1. One member with no devices (an account that left WhatsApp) no longer fails the whole group
   offer: discoverGroupParticipants leaves them out with a warning, and placeGroupCall dials only
   the targets that remain (reachableTargets, still at least two).
2. An offer that is already over (is_call_ended, terminate_reason) is ignored before the group
   branch, which had no such check: a group call that rang while the engine was off was
   preaccepted and rung as live. The 1:1 path had the check already; it moved into isEndedOffer.
3. Audio of payload type 121 is MLow in a SplitRed (RED) container: group-call peers switch to it
   after their first packets, and decoded as a bare frame it was 10 ms of silence (0.0.1.248's
   diagnostics). DecodeAudio, the one decode path of 1:1 and group calls, sets the decoder's
   redundancy from the payload type. It also logs each participant's first payloads (debug, 249).
4. Group playout popped and dropped words (0.0.1.251): the mixer sent nothing while nobody spoke, so
   the sink ran dry; a pause's frame decoded to 10 ms for its packet's 60; and 120 ms in, 240 ms at
   most was short of the ~125 ms the packets arrive off pace. Now silence keeps the pace, a short
   decode is padded to the frame, and the queues fill 180 ms and hold 480.
Tests: TestReachableTargetsDropsUsersDiscoveryLeftOut, TestIsEndedOffer.

